          "question": "e-8224",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,.$*\n\n- the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n\n- $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n\n- addition of polynomials is not commutative",
